<section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">The forms we ask you to fill in</h2>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        When you come to work with Jewel Bespoke Build or Jewel Property Serve — as an employee, as a
        self-employed individual or as a sub-contracting company — we ask you to fill in forms on this
        portal: the HMRC new starter checklist, a right to work form, an emergency contact form, a
        workstation assessment, a company vehicle form, your training certificates, a sub-contractor
        questionnaire and insurance updates, and a vehicle accident report if you have an accident in one
        of our vehicles. You open each one from a link, usually one we send you, on your phone and without
        an account.
    </p>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        Each form carries the name of the Jewel company that asked you for it, and that company is
        responsible for what you send on it: @JewelCompanies.BespokeBuild.LegalName for its own forms and
        @JewelCompanies.PropertyServe.LegalName for its own. Both companies' forms are held here, in this
        portal. Each form says what it is used for; in short, we ask because the law requires it — a right
        to work check before anyone starts, the starter checklist for payroll, the licence check our motor
        insurance needs and the records our health and safety duties need — and to carry out your
        engagement with us.
    </p>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        What you send is read by the office staff who deal with it. Right to work records and the starter
        checklist are kept in their own restricted stores, which only our directors, our compliance
        coordinator and the portal's administrators can open — and, for the starter checklist, our accounts
        team. The two health questions on the emergency contact form are optional; an answer is shown only
        when someone who may see it asks to, and each time it is seen is recorded. The copy of a form we
        email back to you leaves out reference numbers, your date of birth, identity and licence details and
        your driving record. Once we have checked your driving licence we delete the photograph of it and
        keep only whether you meet our insurance criteria.
    </p>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        A right to work record is kept for two years after you stop working for us. The starter checklist,
        your training certificates and the other forms a person sends are kept for six years after you stop
        working for us; a company vehicle form for six years after the vehicle comes back; a sub-contracting
        company's questionnaire and insurance certificates for six years after its last form. The files from
        a form you started but never sent are removed after eighteen months. On its date a form is destroyed
        — its answers and its files — and the destruction is recorded.
    </p>
</section>
